- F-34 **Under the switch-over's setting the code generator refused 52 declarations of the library's twelve components, all of them declarations that the checker passes, measured once before it compiled a `where` clause in a declaration's own header.** Measured with the checker's failures caught per declaration and the bound `Any`, the distance stage's setting: `FortressLibrary` 28, `RangeInternals` 11, `List` and `String` 5 each, and `FlatString`, `Stream` and `NatReflect` 1 each. A declaration counts at its first wall, and no emitted class was run. Four of the 52 met a `where` clause in their own header as their first wall. The code generator now compiles such a clause (F-181), so the present count is not measured. Each kind has a ledger row; the kinds include a local function (row 304), varargs (row 624), `asif` (row 818) and "Not in the trait table" (row 733). Measured once on an earlier base, the dispatch generator refused none of `FortressLibrary`'s 178 overload sets. No test checks it, since the gate's distance stage runs no code generation. Detail: `reviews/phase3-exit/zero-audit.md`, "Part C. The debt carried into phase 4", item 4; `perf-probes/codegen-distance/REPORT.md`, sections 2 to 6.
