- F-298 **A `builtinPrimitive` body whose string names a static helper of `nativeHelpers/` compiles on the compiled path as a call of that helper.** At the parse, in a compile and in the gate's count and distance stages but not under walk, a body that is exactly `builtinPrimitive("pkg.Class.method")`, its string under `com.sun.fortress.nativeHelpers.` and naming a public static method, becomes a call through a synthetic `import java` of the helper, `self` first for a method of a trait or object. So the checker checks the declaration against the helper's Java signature (P-58). The rewrite reaches only a component's top-level declarations and its traits' and objects' members: such a body in a local function or in an object expression's method stays a call of `builtinPrimitive`, and its compile stops 'Variable builtinPrimitive is not defined.', where walk runs it (row 865). A string under that package that names no public static method is a static error at the string, 'builtinPrimitive names no static helper: …'. In the two stages, which check the one library, every other string, the glue classes among them, stays a call of `builtinPrimitive[\T\](javaClass:String):T`, which the checker types at the declared return type, against no Java signature; so does a declaration with a varargs parameter (row 849). In a compile, both stop 'Variable builtinPrimitive is not defined.' In the stages the checker reads the helper's Java types as the one library's, `int` as `ZZ32` and `String` as `String`, as walk reads a written `import java` (F-180; row 845). Where the declaration gives `NN32`, `NN64` or `Char` to a position that the checker reads as `ZZ32` or `ZZ64`, the rewrite puts the matching transfer helper around that argument or around the call, so the checker reads the composition (F-308). Such a body compiles to the same bytes as a written `import java` alias call, through the helper's generated wrapper (F-301). Test: `compiler_tests/NativeHelperBindingCompiled`, with `XXXNativeHelperMisfitCompiled`, `XXXNativeHelperMisspeltCompiled` and `XXXNativeHelperOutsidePackageCompiled`; the reading in the stages, `NamingCzarJUTest.testForeignOneLibrary`. Detail: `compile-ladder/rung-natives-compiled/REPORT.md`, "What changed and why".
