- F-306 **Under walk, 20 of trait `ZZ64`'s native bindings and 16 of trait `ZZ`'s name helpers of `nativeHelpers/`, keep every value the glue classes gave, and their `DIV` by zero throws `DivisionByZero`.** The 36 name 28 helpers of `simpleLongArith`, `simpleIntArith`, `simpleUnsignedLongArith` and `simpleArbitraryPrecisionArith`, those that the compiler's prelude binds for the same operations; `ZZ64`'s four wrapping bindings name the wrapping helpers that the prelude binds under its `BOX` spellings (row 348). `longOverflowingDiv` and `div` raise the library's `DivisionByZero` under walk (F-24). `REM` and `MOD` still name glue classes and end the run at a zero divisor: on `ZZ64` row 336, on `ZZ` row 848. A `ZZ` helper takes only a `BigNum` value, since walk's loader unboxes a `BigInteger` by `getBigInteger`; walk's coercions convert another integer operand first. Test: `tests/NativeHelperFamilyIntegersWalk.fss`, `tests/ZZ64DivisionByZeroWalk.fss`, `tests/ZZDivisionByZeroWalk.fss`, `compiler_tests/NativeHelperFamilyIntegersCompiled`. Detail: `compile-ladder/rung-natives-integers/REPORT.md`, "What changed and why".
